<h1>Connect ShipStation Custom Store</h1><p>In your own ShipStation account, add a Selling Channel → Custom Store. Enter these details there.</p>
<section class="card"><div class="card-body stack"><label>Custom Store endpoint<input class="input" readonly value="<%= endpoint %>"></label><label>Username<input class="input" readonly value="<%= setup.username %>" autocomplete="off"></label><label>Password<input class="input" type="password" readonly value="<%= setup.password %>" autocomplete="off"></label>
<p>Map <strong>awaiting_shipment</strong> to Awaiting Shipment and <strong>shipped</strong> to Shipped. Each prepared single-package StockChief parcel is one ShipStation order, identified by its parcel number.</p>
<p>Multi-package parcels use the connected shipping API. This connection exports packed parcel contents and the customer’s shipping address. Final invoices, discounts and taxes stay in StockChief. Tracking notifications update the parcel; they do not confirm physical handoff or deduct stock.</p>
<p>Your connection password is stored encrypted and belongs only to this inventory. Open this owner-only setup again to copy it when needed.</p><form method="post" action="/settings/shipping/shipstation-custom/disconnect"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="connectorId" value="<%= setup.connectorId %>"><button class="btn btn--ghost">Disconnect Custom Store</button></form><a class="btn" href="/settings/shipping">Back to shipping settings</a></div></section>
